  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of shrub}}\n{{speciesbox\n| genus = Philadelphus\n| species = incanus\n| authority = Koehne\n}}\n\n'''''Philadelphus incanus''''', the '''hairy mock orange''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=PHIN33|taxon=Philadelphus incanus|accessdate=24 September 2015}}</ref> is a deciduous shrub in the genus ''[[Philadelphus]]''.  Native to [[China]], it is a medium to large shrub characterised by its hairy leaves and later flowering than other members of the genus.\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n*The Hillier Manual of Trees and Shrubs, Ed. John Hillier, David & Charles 2007, {{ISBN|978-0-7153-2664-0}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q2314775}}\n\n[[Category:Philadelphus|incanus]]\n\n\n{{cornales-stub}}",
